body: |-
  ## Files created
  - packages/paradigm/src/commands/override.ts — three subcommand handlers (overrideClearOne, overrideList, overrideClearAll) + shared archiveRemediation + appendOverrideEvent helpers

  ## Files modified
  - packages/paradigm/src/commands/internal/active-remediations.ts (lines 30-60, 95-115) — non-behavioral refactor: extracted pure getActiveRemediations(cwd) helper + exported RemediationOutput type. Existing activeRemediationsCommand consumes the helper. Hook output bytes unchanged.
  - packages/paradigm/src/index.ts (lines 2749-2778) — registered public `override [id]` command with `list` and `clear-all --force` subcommands via lazy dynamic imports
  - packages/paradigm/src/commands/.purpose — added paradigm-override-cli symbol

  ## Subcommand pattern
  **Direct import** (recommended path from spec §12). overrideList calls getActiveRemediations() in-process — no subprocess overhead, no subprocess error surface, single source of truth for the parsing logic shared between Stop hook helper command and the override CLI.

  ## Manual smoke verification
  - `override list` (empty) → JSON `[]`
  - `override list` (1 fixture) → JSON array with expected fields
  - `override rmd-test123` → exit 0, archived_at stamp added, file moved to .archived/, JSONL row written with mechanism: cli
  - `override rmd-doesnotexist` → exit 1, error message
  - `override clear-all` → exit 1, requires --force
  - `override clear-all --force` → cleared all, one event row per

  ## Advisor catches
  1. Double-checkmark in success output stripped (success() helper already prepends ✓)
  2. Explicit process.exit(1) after error() calls (error() doesn't terminate)
  3. Atomic fs.rename for archive (not copy+unlink — matters for crash safety)

  ## Wave 4 prerequisites
  - CLAUDE.md "Agent-Owned Soft-Blocks (v6.1)" subsection insertion (spec §8)
  - CHANGELOG.md placeholder for next version
  - Note that archived_at audit trail is now visible on cleared YAML
  - paradigm override is public — listed in `paradigm --help`
